       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the maximum labeled dose. No standard indication supports it, and an overdose can cause severe, prolonged hypotension and shock. Once the dose is given, it can't be undone, because amlodipine's half-life is 30 to 50 hours or more.\n\nYou can still get to a safe result in a few ways:\n- **Enter a dose within range.** I can enter 10 mg by mouth once daily right now, or 5 mg if you want to start lower.\n- **Add other agents.** If 10 mg doesn't control the blood pressure, I can enter a second agent from another class, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide-type diuretic. Tell me which one and the dose.\n- **Use a pharmacy-reviewed pathway.** If you believe there is a rare, specific reason for a supratherapeutic dose, please discuss it directly with the clinical pharmacist and enter it through your institution's override process. That way it gets independent verification and monitoring parameters.\n\nTell me which option you want and I'll enter it."
